Implemented US-032's first unmet gap (AC3 server-side CAS) plus AC5 docs.

**Server** (`a2e-documents`): two additive nullable `document` fields (`contentRevision` head token, `contentBaseRevision` expected token); pure `document-revision-cas.ts` (13 node cases); `guard-document-revision-save` logic function on `document.updated`/`updatedFields:['content']` that repairs a stale committed write in place (SDK has no pre-write hook), stamping a `repair-` sentinel base so it never re-repairs.

**Front**: `persistBlocknoteBody` writes both tokens on the same update; the save-conflict guard tracks the base revision, captures the conflicting one, and `Keep my changes`/`Use saved version` resolve against it (retry test added). Non-editor writers stay last-write-wins.

**Docs**: a2e-documents README "Concurrent saves" section with single-writer guidance; corrected the audit tradeoff row.

Checks green: app test 13/13, typecheck, lint, `dev:build` (22 files); front co-editing 27 tests, related 135 tests, `tsgo` exit 0, oxlint/oxfmt clean; `check-docs` PASS. Reported `done-for-review`, Ready-to-tick: no — Tier-2 reinstall + two-session browser proof remain (orchestrator). Phase report and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` appended.

